+# Free-Text Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope; Filtering the Directory Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. Its provenance stayed open, like every Non-Goals row the owner had not yet decided.
+
+A request to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty reached NG-9 on 2026-09-29. Read literally, the row covers that request, because narrowing a list is a form of finding veterinarians. The owner decided the row at intake instead of letting the request settle it by implication. The decision, quoted verbatim:
+
+> Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in. Record the narrowing the way the project records non-goal changes.
+
+The same intake reinstated the machine-readable veterinarian list as a supported surface under a fresh requirement. The withdrawn `REQ-VET-002` stays withdrawn.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Rejected by the owner: it would decline a filter over data the directory already shows.
+2. **Drop NG-9 for veterinarians.** Rejected by the owner: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text search for a veterinarian stays declined. Filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 declines searching for a pet or a visit, and free-text searching for a veterinarian. It no longer declines filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute the directory already shows. The first such filter is narrowing by specialty.
+
+The pet and visit parts of the row are unchanged and stay part of the open provenance consultation.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Narrowing the directory by specialty is in scope and is requested now.
+- Filtering by another attribute the directory shows needs no further non-goal change. It still needs its own request.
+- A request for free-text veterinarian search proceeds only on a new owner decision recorded at intake. The request itself never reopens the row.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the preamble.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the requirement the narrowing admits.
