+# Narrowed Veterinarian Directory Reads Bypass the Vet Cache
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`REQ-VET-003` lets both veterinarian directory routes be narrowed by a specialty named in the address. Every unnarrowed read of the directory goes through the vet cache. That cache is declared through the JCache API with no size limit and no eviction. Its paged read is already keyed by the caller's page request.
+
+A narrowed read carries a caller-supplied string. Letter case alone yields many spellings of one specialty, and any name the clinic lacks is still a valid request. Caching narrowed reads would key an unbounded cache by arbitrary caller text.
+
+The seeded directory holds six veterinarians and three specialties. No latency requirement exists for either route.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Cache narrowed reads by the requested name.** Repeat reads are cheap. The cache gains one entry per distinct spelling any caller sends, with no bound. That is a memory-exhaustion lever on an open route.
+2. **Cache the normalized name.** Lower-casing folds the case variants. Unknown names still add entries without bound.
+3. **Filter the cached full list in memory and page it by hand.** Needs no new query. The page arithmetic is hand-written where Spring Data already pages, and matching moves out of the repository.
+4. **Uncached derived query** (chosen). Each narrowed request runs one query. The repository owns matching and paging, and the cache key space stays as it was.
+
+## Decision
+
+Narrowed directory reads go through `VetRepository` derived queries that carry no cache annotation. Unnarrowed reads keep their existing caching. A later slice that adds another caller-keyed read of the directory follows the same rule until the vet cache gains a size limit.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A narrowed request always costs one database query. At the recorded directory size this is negligible.
+- A request cannot grow the cache, whatever specialty it names.
+- The unbounded page-keyed entries remain a pre-existing gap, tracked as the survey's open question on the vet cache.
+- Caching narrowed reads becomes possible once the cache has a size limit, through a new decision that supersedes this one.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md — Narrowing the veterinarian directory](../system-design.md#contracts)
+- [system-design.md — Scale and Load](../system-design.md#scale-and-load)
